<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Wheat Pool sees good wheat grade.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Wheat Pool sees good wheat grade.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Wheat Pool on Thursday forecast most of the province's 14.5 million acres of spring wheat will be rated in the top grade.</p>
<p>About 89 percent of spring wheat was expected to grade No1 Canada Western Red Spring, assuming favourable weather for the rest of harvest.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan Agriculture said the provincial 10-year average has 47 percent of spring wheat grading No1 CWRS.</p>
<p>No frost damage was reported anywhere in Saskatchewan by Sept 9 even though temperatures dropped to -3.0 Celsius for one hour around Wadena on Sept 7.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
